  "headline": "The City of Palaces",
  "short_description": "Mysuru (Mysore) is famed for its opulent palace, silk sarees and grand Dasara festival celebrations.",
  "about": "Former capital of the Wadiyar dynasty, Mysuru is known across India for its illuminated Mysore Palace and its role as the historic centre of Dasara celebrations.\n\nLocated in southern Karnataka on the Deccan Plateau.\n\nKnown for Mysore silk, sandalwood crafts, yoga tradition (Ashtanga Vinyasa) and classical dance.\n\nPredominantly Hindu, home to the Chamundeshwari Temple atop Chamundi Hill.",
  "history": "Seat of the Wadiyar kings of the Kingdom of Mysore for centuries, with a break under Hyder Ali and Tipu Sultan in the 18th century.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Mysore Airport (airport)\n- Mysuru Junction (railway)\n- Mysuru City Bus Stand (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Kannada, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to March (Dasara in September/October is a highlight)",
  "ideal_duration_text": "1–2 days",
  "nearest_airport": "Mysore Airport (MYQ), limited service; Kempegowda International Airport (BLR) more connected",
  "nearest_railway_station": "Mysuru Junction",
